      "id": "claim_1f29f6a840d34e1ca4adb2d184d49419",
      "statement": "Activation restores the cell's SQLite from the newest safe source (local eviction snapshot vs replicated bucket) chosen by a pure core predicate, and the RuntimeManager owns V8 handles and paths but never lifecycle policy: StartRuntime, Publish, and StopRuntime effects decide when a cell handle becomes dispatchable.",
